From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brewie BSP <bsp@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 14:58:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wiring: skip initial drain with external reset

When noautoreset is selected, reset is controlled externally.  Draining the
UART after that reset can consume the bootloader's startup traffic and adds a
250 ms idle interval before STK500v2 SIGN_ON.  The B20 bootloader needs the
first request at a precise time after reset, so do not drain in this mode.

Signed-off-by: Brewie BSP <bsp@example.invalid>
---
 src/wiring.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/wiring.c b/src/wiring.c
--- a/src/wiring.c
+++ b/src/wiring.c
@@ -179,1 +179,2 @@
-  stk500v2_drain(pgm, 0);
+  if(!mywiring.noautoreset)
+    stk500v2_drain(pgm, 0);
